=== contains(x, /re/) and id:~ and id >= 3
kind: events  source: logs  limit: 200
canonical: contains(x, "/re/") and id:"~" and id >= 3
sql: SELECT timestamp, id, stream, level, level_num, service, environment, host, message_template, message, exception, event_type, trace_id, span_id, protocol, connection_id, props_json FROM tidemark.events WHERE timestamp >= ? AND timestamp < ? AND ((positionCaseInsensitiveUTF8(props[?], ?) > 0 AND id = toUUIDOrZero(?)) AND ifNull(toFloat64OrNull(toString(id)) >= ?, 0)) ORDER BY timestamp DESC, id DESC LIMIT ?
args:
  0: time 2026-10-13T11:00:00Z
  1: time 2026-10-13T12:00:00Z
  2: string "x"
  3: string "/re/"
  4: string "~"
  5: float64 3
  6: int 200
columns: timestamp:time, id:string, stream:string, level:string, level_num:number, service:string, environment:string, host:string, message_template:string, message:string, exception:string, event_type:string, trace_id:string, span_id:string, protocol:string, connection_id:string, props_json:json

=== * | where level:error | stats count() by host span auto | sort @bucket desc
kind: timeseries  source: logs  limit: 10000  span: 1m0s
canonical: * | where level:"error" | stats count() by host span auto | sort @bucket desc
sql: SELECT toStartOfInterval(timestamp, toIntervalSecond(?)) AS bucket, host AS g0, count() AS a0 FROM tidemark.events WHERE timestamp >= ? AND timestamp < ? AND (level_num = ?) GROUP BY bucket, g0 ORDER BY bucket ASC, g0 ASC LIMIT ?
args:
